"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"kind","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Kind","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLGlyphV4Kinda","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlglyph\/kind-swift.property","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLGlyph\/kind-swift.property","abstract":[{"text":"The type of glyph being defined.","type":"text"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLGlyph/Kind-swift.typealias":{"title":"MXLGlyph.Kind","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"typealias","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Kind","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlglyph\/kind-swift.typealias","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLGlyph\/Kind-swift.typealias","abstract":[{"text":"The glyph-type defines what type of glyph is being defined in a glyph element. Values include quarter-rest,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"g-clef-ottava-bassa, c-clef, f-clef, percussion-clef, octave-shift-up-8, octave-shift-down-8, octave-shift-","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"continue-8, octave-shift-down-15, octave-shift-up-15, octave-shift-continue-15, octave-shift-down-22, octave-","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"shift-up-22, and octave-shift-continue-22. This is left as a string so that other application-specific types","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"can be defined, but it is made a separate type so that it can be redefined more strictly.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Kind","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLGlyph":{"abstract":[{"text":"The glyph element represents what SMuFL glyph should be used for different variations of symbols that are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"semantically identical. The type attribute specifies what type of glyph is being defined. The element value","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"specifies what SMuFL glyph to use, including recommended stylistic alternates. The SMuFL glyph name should","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"match the type. For instance, a type of quarter-rest would use values restQuarter, restQuarterOld, or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"restQuarterZ. A type of g-clef-ottava-bassa would use values gClef8vb, gClef8vbOld, or gClef8vbCClef. A type","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of octave-shift-up-8 would use values ottava, ottavaBassa, ottavaBassaBa, ottavaBassaVb, or octaveBassa.","type":"text"}],"title":"MXLGlyph","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLGlyph","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLGlyph","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlglyph","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLGlyph"}}}